# Toronto Rising — dashboard testing

Run from `.dev/storyteller-dashboard/`: `npm test` (Vitest). Also part of `npm run build` via `npm run typecheck` plus tests in CI-local `npm test` before calling dashboard work done.

## What to test where

| Layer | Tool | Examples |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Pure logic | **Vitest** (node or jsdom) | `sceneKeyFromTitle`, occupancy helpers, payload builders |
| React shell | **Vitest** + Testing Library | tabs exist, Storyteller-only chrome, no player HUD |
| Visual board / GSAP / layout | **Playwright MCP** headed Chrome (`user-playwright`) in the dedicated TorontoRising profile, no extension debugger bar. Follow [playwright-browser-focus](toronto-rising-playwright-browser-focus.mdc) and [PLAYWRIGHT.md](../../.dev/storyteller-dashboard/PLAYWRIGHT.md). Do not attach via `--extension`. |

Do **not** add Save & Play or in-TTS playbooks for dashboard-only CSS/React. If the change also edits Lua import/bridge, use the existing TTS playbooks for that Lua side.

## Policy

- New pure functions get a Vitest file next to them (`*.test.ts` / `*.test.tsx`).
- Do not unit-test GSAP pointer paths; cover those in Playwright when the board behavior changes.
- Mock `init*` tab boots in React shell tests so they do not hit the network.
- Do **not** wrap the dashboard in React StrictMode while vanilla `init*` functions still bind DOM listeners.
